# Renders and derived artifacts are never committed — they are reproducible by
# definition (ARCHITECTURE.md §6).
#
# ORDER MATTERS: git applies the *last* matching pattern, so every `!` exception
# has to come after the `*.png` that would otherwise swallow it. A negation
# written above it is silently inert — which is how the baked plates ended up
# with a committed manifest and no frames.
out/
media/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.png

# Layout previews ARE committed — they are how a shot gets reviewed in every
# format, and they cost nothing to store.
!docs/**/*.png
!docs/previews/*.svg
!docs/previews/render/*.png
!src/**/*.png

# Baked Tier-2 plates ARE committed, and this is load-bearing: a plate is the
# output of a Blender bake that may have happened years ago, so shipping the
# frames is what keeps Blender a build-time dependency instead of a runtime one.
# Without them an episode that uses a plate cannot render at all.
!assets/plates/**/*.png

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
dist/
build/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# JavaScript (renderers/three, experiences/, episodes/*/three) — CONVENTIONS §14a
node_modules/
.vite/

# Voiceover audio is a local input, never committed: timing comes from the
# committed timeline/words.json, and episode.yaml pins the audio's sha256 so a
# missing or re-recorded file fails loudly at compose time.
episodes/*/audio/
